            <ArticleTitle>Impaired vascular responses to nitroglycerin in subjects with coronary atherosclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-9, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To study smooth muscle function in atherosclerosis, we calculated dose-response curves in patients with coronary artery disease and in controls by measuring changes in brachial artery diameter after incremental sublingual doses of nitroglycerin. The doses required to produce a 50% maximal dilator response were significantly higher in patients with coronary artery disease than in controls (p &lt;0.002), suggesting smooth muscle dysfunction in atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
